# power-refutation: this class named TestRaftExitCriteria when it was declared -- a 10,000-seed sweep, 19 hours per invocation at the exit run's measured 6.9 s/seed. Seven mutants named it, so make mutants asked for six days of machine time for that covering test alone, and make mutants is in the ci target. Declaring a sweep as a covering test is the disease this phase diagnosed twice and then reproduced four times while writing the general form
# mutates: installing a snapshot no longer advances this replica's `applied`, so the state machine moves forward and the number that says where it is does not. raft's own appliedIdx IS advanced on install, so this restores a shadowed fact maintained on one path and not the other -- the same family as a census counter incremented both in a caller and in the function extracted out of it, except that this one reads LOW. Low is not harmless: serveReadyReads waits on it, so a read the snapshot already covers waits for a committed entry that may never arrive on a quiet range; and the ledger records it as AppliedAt, so read-index-answers-match-the-log replays the committed log to a position BELOW the node's real state and reports a correct answer as stale. It is killed by that oracle -- as a FALSE ACCUSATION of a correct answer, which is the shape this class always takes and the reason it went three phases unnoticed: nothing in the tree compared a node's claimed position against its actual state, and the oracle that could compare them derived both sides from the same understated number until BUG-028's fix made the model read the latest version instead
